# What: Manifest Content Type Rule. Why: Netlify serves .webmanifest files as application/octet-stream, which Chrome tolerates but Firefox and some install paths reject. How: This forces the manifest's correct type.
/manifest.webmanifest
	Content-Type: application/manifest+json



# _headers = Security Headers Policy
#
# @summary
# Hardening headers applied to every response. Every script, style, font, and
# icon is self-hosted, the support form's Netlify Forms POST
# (tabs/settings/contact-support.tsx) goes to this same origin, and the only
# third parties are Firebase and the reCAPTCHA Enterprise check its App Check
# runs, for the optional paid sync. That lets the Content-Security-Policy stay
# strict, naming each address rather than allowing broad ones: Firestore, which
# holds the cloud copy, the two auth services that sign in and renew tokens,
# App Check's token exchange, and reCAPTCHA's own requests (connect-src), the
# project's own auth domain, whose hidden frame runs Google sign-in's pop-up,
# and reCAPTCHA's frames (frame-src), and Google's API loader that the sign-in
# frame needs, plus reCAPTCHA's scripts (script-src). The reCAPTCHA addresses
# are the ones Google's reCAPTCHA FAQ lists for a CSP. None of it loads unless
# someone uses an account.
#
# default-src 'self' is the fallback every unlisted directive inherits, so
# font-src, img-src, manifest-src, and worker-src need no lines of their
# own. The directives listed either need a different value than 'self'
# (connect-src, object-src, frame-src, script-src, style-src), are never
# covered by default-src at all (frame-ancestors, form-action), or just
# state the default for clarity (base-uri).
#
# style-src needs 'unsafe-inline' for two reasons: the boot splash's
# critical CSS in index.html is inline on purpose, since an external
# stylesheet would add a network round trip before it can paint, and React
# renders many components' dynamic sizing and positioning through inline
# style attributes (e.g. src/ui/bg-flourish.tsx). Both fall under style-src,
# not script-src, so this doesn't weaken protection against inline scripts.
# The boot splash's dismiss script is its own file (public/boot-splash.js)
# precisely so script-src needs no such allowance.
#
# Strict-Transport-Security keeps browsers on HTTPS for two years across every
# subdomain (Netlify already sends www to the bare domain over HTTPS, and
# Cloudflare passes the redirect through), replacing Netlify's default of one
# year for this host only. It leaves out preload, which commits the domain to
# the browsers' built-in HTTPS list and is slow to undo. Referrer-Policy sends
# a referrer only to this same origin, so the outbound links (the legal
# generators, the support site, GitHub) never learn which page a visitor came
# from. Permissions-Policy turns off every powerful browser feature the app
# never uses, leaving the ones it does (the clipboard, storage, the service
# worker, and notifications, which no policy covers) untouched.
#
# @author z4nta0 <https://github.com/z4nta0>

# What: Security Headers Rule. Why: Every response should refuse framing, sniffing, plain HTTP, unused browser features, and anything loaded from another origin. How: This applies the Content-Security-Policy, the permissions and referrer policies, HSTS, a nosniff content type, and a deny on framing to every path.
/*
	Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://content-firebaseappcheck.googleapis.com https://firestore.googleapis.com https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com https://securetoken.googleapis.com https://www.google.com/recaptcha/; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; frame-src https://ease-my-life-4ce18.firebaseapp.com https://recaptcha.google.com/recaptcha/ https://www.google.com/recaptcha/; object-src 'none'; script-src 'self' https://apis.google.com https://www.google.com/recaptcha/ https://www.gstatic.com/recaptcha/; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'
	Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), browsing-topics=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), fullscreen=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), hid=(), idle-detection=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), picture-in-picture=(), publickey-credentials-get=(), screen-wake-lock=(), serial=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
	Referrer-Policy: same-origin
	Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
	X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
	X-Frame-Options: DENY
